      "message": "\u003e \u003e \u003e I changed it to `__wasm__`, as both wasm32 and wasm64 support the u64 type.\n\u003e \u003e \u003e \n\u003e \u003e \n\u003e \u003e 32-bit arm supports a 64-bit type too, but here we\u0027re trying to align to a natural register size. Do you have any 32-bit devices (like a chromebook for example) to test this change on?\n\u003e \u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e If you want to try to run a 32-bit binary on a 64-bit machine that would be helpful. Otherwise, I think it\u0027s simpler to make this target 64-bit only to start with. 32-bit can be enabled in another patch.\n\nLet\u0027s just go with `__wasm64__` to get these landed.",
